  "body": "## Problem and behavior\n\nLegacy followers, following and friends GETs returned names and relationship metadata without canonical block/closure checks. They now filter whole rows using the shared profile policy and current bearer authority in one database snapshot. URLs/DTOs, directed history, NFC provenance and UTC dates are preserved; tied timestamps now have deterministic ID order. Historical mutual follows remain distinct from accepted connection consent.\n\nLegacy friend-of-friend suggestions expose inferred counts from edges one actor can manufacture, without disclosure consent. Their existing DTO cannot express a safer reason accurately. Preserve that endpoint only before activation with no canonical pair/closure state anywhere; afterward return an empty array, including during pause, and use the separate Discover view for recommendations.\n\n## Dependencies and review order\n\nDepends on draft #397 at `7c452efcb`, which depends on #390. #394 holds consolidated verification evidence. No other branch was merged. Review the additive SQL and small adapters, then the model/HTTP tests; generated SQL cases and evidence logs are separate files. Remains draft while wider writer/client/identity integrations and this branch's hosted CI are unfinished.\n\n## Actual local verification\n\n- TLC safety/progress: 76,624 generated / 24,192 distinct states; three unsafe variants fail their intended invariants.\n- **8,064** observed model cases pass PostgreSQL. Unsafe row-policy and suggestion-count controls fail cases 229 and 272. Read-function STABLE classification and UTC behavior are asserted.\n- Actual bearer/PostgreSQL HTTP: **116 examples, zero failures**, including 12 new relationship cases.\n- Full Stack: **2,542 examples, zero failures**; application executable built. Catalog audit exit 0.\n- Complete PostgreSQL 17 schema: additive apply/reapply, post-migration source write and pause preserve stored history while denying its blocked projection.\n- Synthetic SQL benchmark: 10,005 accounts; degree 100 p95 3.43\u20133.63ms and degree 10,004 p95 214.10\u2013255.01ms, within predeclared 250/1500ms bounds. Paired reference is an unprotected join, not the complete old handler. Initial benchmark fixture left an organization identity active; equality assertions caught it and the all-eligible fixture was corrected without weakening checks.\n- Hosted CI for this branch is pending. Parent #397 full CI succeeded after one unchanged mocked-browser rerun; the original timeout is retained, not called a pass.\n\n## Migration, flags and rollback\n\nApply `2026-09-15_social_v2_relationship_reads.sql` after #397 prerequisites, before serving this application against the foundation. Adds three STABLE functions and an incoming-edge index; no data rewrite, backfill, new infrastructure or production flag activation. The index build takes a write-conflicting lock: measure large-table rollout and prepare it concurrently if needed before the transactional migration.\n\nNo foundation retains legacy compatibility; an incomplete foundation fails closed with 503. Existing process/database gates remain inactive in production. Pause retains authorization adapters, activation memory and source data. Never restore old readers/drop enforcement after activation; retain the adapters in a rollback build or disable the affected routes. Old instances and requests must be drained before future activation. No down migration deletes post-migration writes.\n\n## Limits and handoff\n\n[Policy, research, model traceability, evidence, reproduction and operational steps](https://github.com/diegueins680/tdf-app/blob/feat/social-relationship-read-boundary-20260915/docs/social/relationship-read-boundary.md).\n\nExisting array contracts remain unpaginated and grow with degree; no unlimited-scale claim. Legacy suggestion fanout remains only in the pre-enforcement compatibility stage. Old friend/vCard mutations and their response DTOs still need consent-preserving authorization. Client cutover/cache withdrawal, other search/media/notification surfaces, delegated entities and lifecycle/moderation integration remain incomplete. No merge, deployment or production activation. The historical provider-triggered deployment exception remains unresolved.\n",
